PDF.js is distributed under the Apache License 2.0. Its license is included
with the built browser assets at dist/browser/pdfjs/LICENSE. Included CMaps,
standard fonts, WASM and ICC assets retain their accompanying license files.
Native bibliography conversion bundles Citation.js and its dependencies;
notices and a version manifest are retained at dist/licenses/. The name/date
helper packages omit separate license files; their published MIT declarations,
author metadata and the Citation.js project MIT notice are retained explicitly.
Embedded CSL styles/locales retain their own rights metadata.

CSL citation processing uses citeproc-js 2.4.63, copyright (c) 2009-2019
Frank Bennett, under its CPAL-1.0 option, not this project's MIT license.
citeproc-js implements the Citation Style Language: https://citationstyles.org/
The unmodified upstream source is distributed at dist/vendor/citeproc.cjs and
at dist/browser/licenses/citeproc/source.txt. The complete CPAL license, source
revision and integration notice are retained at dist/licenses/citeproc/;
the browser attribution links to the source and license within browserRoot.
No modification or minification is applied to the separately loaded engine.
Server PDF text extraction bundles unpdf (MIT) and its embedded PDF.js parser
(Apache License 2.0), independently of the browser renderer version.
No research PDFs, source notes or user annotations are distributed.
